Z","body":"+1 to add and fine with suggested name/id unless anyone has a strong reason to use something different\n\n@karsten-klein - do you have any idea as to whether the missing word in the first sentence is a typo or as found in the wild?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2686937859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2687695145","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2609#issuecomment-2687695145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2609","id":2687695145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86gMvkp","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T11:36:34Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T11:36:34Z","body":"I do note that there's a couple differences between this one, and what Scancode calls \"dante-treglia\":\n* this one starts \"This **software** is provided\", Scancode's starts \"This is provided\"\n* this one has quotation marks around \"as is\", Scancode's doesn't\n\nBoth of those could likely be handled by markup if the general consensus is to treat those as non-substantive changes. (This would be my view.)\n\nFor the name / ID, I went down a rabbit hole trying to figure out where this originated. As best I can tell, it looks like it came from a source code CD provided with the book \"Game Programming Gems 2\". CD ISO is on the Internet Archive at https://archive.org/details/game-programming-gems-2-disk-iso, and it can be seen on Github at e.g. https://github.com/alecnunn/bookresources/blob/4562f6430af5afffde790c42d0f3a33176d8003b/GameDevelopment/Game%20Programming%20Gems%202/SourceCode/06%20Audio%20Programming/05%20Patterson/Win32.cpp#L8.\n\nIt looks like multiple author names were sometimes used with this license, not just Dante Treglia. I also just tend to prefer avoiding using individuals' names as part of the license name and ID, where we don't have to.\n\nSo perhaps something like `Game-Programming-Gems` for the ID and \"Game Programming Gems License\" for the name? This would be somewhat comparable to [`Graphics-Gems`](https://spdx.org/licenses/Graphics-Gems.html) which is on the list today.\n\nBut I don't feel particularly strongly about this -- can live with the original proposed name/ID if others prefer.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2687695145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2691810842","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2609#issuecomment-2691810842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2609","id":2691810842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86gccYa","